# Implementation plan — Spec 1.13.0

## Summary

Add **Settings → All Companies** (`/settings/companies`) for normal WebOnOne users. Page is a standard UI Kit list (`FeaturePage` + `ListPageBody` + ItemList). Users register **one or multiple** companies via the existing 3-step wizard. Every registration is created with status **`pending`** and Identity role **`company_admin` (Company Owner)** for that company. Only a super admin may set **`approved`** or **`rejected`** from top-level **Companies**. Each list row has a **3-dot menu** with **Login** — enabled for **approved** companies the user owns — which reissues the session as company owner for that `companyId`. Upgrade UI Kit **Tags** tab with **company status tags** (`StatusTag`) and use them on All Companies + super-admin Companies lists. Backend adds `GET /company/me/companies`; register must allow additional companies. Migrate register UX off Basic Settings.

See [02](./02-settings-all-companies-nav.md), [03](./03-my-companies-list-ui.md), [04](./04-multi-company-api.md), [05](./05-ui-kit-company-status-tags.md), [06-company-owner-login.md](./06-company-owner-login.md).

